f the falsely consequential and poor in expression.","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[3,12],[68,77],[116,125]],"translation":"He only remembered his face as he remembered all the faces he had ever seen; but he remembered, too, that it was one of the faces laid by in his memory in the immense class of the falsely consequential and poor in expression.","bold_translation_offsets":[[8,18],[34,44],[84,94]]}],"info_templates":[{"args":{"1":"de","2":":an(acc)/gen<q:higher register><someone/something>"},"name":"+obj","extra_data":{"words":["an","(+","accusative)","(higher","register)","genitive","‘someone/something’"]},"expansion":"[with an (+ accusative) or (higher register) genitive ‘someone/something’]"}],"categories":["German reflexive verbs","German terms with quotations"],"links":[["remember","remember"],["reminded","remind"]],"raw_glosses":["(reflexive) to remember, to be reminded of [with an (+ accusative) or (higher register) genitive ‘someone/something’]"],"glosses":["to remember, to be reminded of"],"tags":["reflexive","weak"]},{"categories":["German colloquialisms","German terms with rare senses","German transitive verbs"],"links":[["remember","remember"],["commemorate","commemorate"]],"raw_glosses":["(transitive, colloquial, rare) to remember, to commemorate"],"glosses":["to remember, to commemorate"],"tags":["colloquial","rare","transitive","weak"]},{"examples":[{"text":"Der nicht unbeträchtliche theoretische Aufwand, der zur Begründung einer Einschränkung der Aufnahmefreiheit getrieben wird, stößt überdies schon deshalb ins Leere, weil die Parteien in aller Regel an der Gewinnung neuer Mitglieder höchlichst interessiert sein werden. Sollte aber eine Partei einen gegenteiligen Kurs verfolgen („klein aber fein“), so ist dagegen aus verfassungsrechtlicher Sicht nur dann etwas zu erinnern, wenn darin ein Indiz für eine gegen die freiheitliche demokratische Grundordnung gerichtete Ausrichtung gesehen werden kann.","ref":"2023, Hans H. Klein, edited by Günt